+(duration)=
+
+### Duration
+
+The {class}`Duration` type converts a length of time into a {class}`datetime.timedelta`. A value is either a whole
+number of seconds, such as `120`, or one or more groups of an integer followed by a unit, such as `1h30m`. The units
+are `d` (days), `h` (hours), `m` (minutes), and `s` (seconds). Each unit may be given at most once and in that
+order, with no spaces between the groups. Units are case-insensitive, so `45S` is the same as `45s`. Negative and
+decimal values are not accepted. A {class}`datetime.timedelta` given as the default is used unchanged.
+
+```{eval-rst}
+.. click:example::
+
+    @click.command()
+    @click.option("--timeout", type=click.Duration(), default="30s", show_default=True)
+    def wait(timeout):
+        click.echo(f"Waiting {timeout.total_seconds():g} seconds.")
+
+.. click:run::
+
+    invoke(wait, args=['--timeout=1h30m'])
+    invoke(wait, args=['--timeout=90'])
+    invoke(wait, args=['--timeout=1.5h'])
+    println()
+    invoke(wait, args=['--help'])
+```
+
+```{versionadded} 8.5.1
+```
+
